From f8b30abadb13c287c1336da07f1ec888348c4ea6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ayiejosh <132535860+ayiejosh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 14:31:08 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 118/294] gallium/pvr: shader stages - create/bind/delete VS
 and FS through pco

create_vs_state and create_fs_state now compile through the linked compiler, so a
shader arriving from the state tracker as NIR comes back as encoded USC microcode,
and bind/delete record and release it:

  shader:       pco encoded 224 bytes of USC for a fragment shader
  shader state: PASS (create_fs_state/bind/delete over NIR)
  --- ALL PASS        (real open kernel module)

Supporting changes:

* shader_caps for vertex and fragment, and supported_irs = NIR per stage so the
  state tracker hands over NIR rather than TGSI. supported_irs is a shader_caps
  field in this Mesa, not a pipe_caps one.
* The numeric caps resources can now honour: max_texture_2d_size from
  rogue_get_render_size_max(), the same device-derived helper the Vulkan driver
  uses. This was deferred in an earlier round precisely because declaring a texture
  size the driver cannot allocate would be a lie; resource creation exists now, so
  it is no longer one.
* Cube, 3D and array are reported ABSENT (0 levels, 1 array layer) because
  resource_create refuses them. Reporting the hardware's full texture capability
  would advertise features the resource code would then reject.
* max_const_buffer0_size matters more than it looks - the state tracker divides it
  by 4 to get MaxUniformComponents, so leaving it zero would give shaders no
  uniforms at all.

Effect on what GL advertises: the four ARB shader extensions now appear
(GL_ARB_vertex_shader, GL_ARB_fragment_shader, GL_ARB_shader_objects,
GL_ARB_shading_language_100) where before there were none.

NOT achieved, and not claimed: the reported GL version is still 1.5 / ES-CM 1.1.
Something outside the shader stage is holding it there and I did not identify
which, so I did not go looking for caps to set until the number moved - that is how
a driver ends up advertising capability it does not have. The shader caps are also
conservative under-claims rather than measured hardware limits, and are marked as
such in the code.
